    {
      "id": "claim_b73eada095bc467eac8f79a076ed8096",
      "statement": "Coverage E in both editions pays damages for which an insured is legally liable because of bodily injury or property damage caused by an occurrence and provides a defense for a covered suit until the applicable occurrence limit is exhausted; Coverage F pays necessary medical expenses without regard to fault when its conditions apply, requires expenses within three years after the accident, and uses a declarations limit per injured person. The 2022-06 Section II additional coverage reduces damage to property of others from $2,500 in 2015-01 to $1,000.",
