    {
      "id": "claim_532f91a1dcda478ca560bafff096b2ab",
      "statement": "The HO-5 claim conditions require prompt notice, theft or criminal-loss reporting to law enforcement when applicable, reasonable mitigation and temporary repairs, preservation and inspection of damaged property, records and inventories, cooperation, and a signed sworn proof of loss within 60 days after request in both editions. Either party may demand appraisal over amount of loss, each appraiser must be selected within 20 days, appraisal does not determine coverage or causation, and payment is due within 60 days after agreement; 2022-06 additionally expressly conditions a duty failure on material prejudice and permits payment delay while material information remains unavailable.",
