    {
      "id": "claim_429ba349ddd744dc9f41ded60e61007e",
      "statement": "HO 05 24 Special Personal Property Coverage changes the policy only as stated, applies policy definitions and conditions otherwise, and controls over conflicting policy language; property ineligible under the policy remains ineligible unless the endorsement provides otherwise. If attached to an HO-5 assembly, it must therefore be read first as the acting document and then with the unchanged HO-5 provisions, but repository metadata identifies HO 05 24 as an HO-3 endorsement rather than an HO-5 form, so attachment and compatibility must be verified. Its stated jewelry-theft limit is $2,500 and it excludes mysterious disappearance among other listed losses.",
      "evidence": [
